+## The dug lake, or {} where it is not dug: {"level", "nodes" (the water), "dug" (node -> floor), "area" (water nodes), "planned" (footprint nodes)}.
+## The level is the lake's spill level (level0). The ground the bowl may take: inside the footprint, joined to the seed, at most maxD over the level, and not the ground beyond a pass: a node whose natural ground is under
+## the level and which the natural flood did not reach (X: the lower ground the water would run to) is never dug, and neither is a node that touches one (the rim: it keeps its height, so the level holds). Digging the
+## rim down is what made the level crawl down a valley's exit; with it kept, a lake on a slope is a pit above its rim, and a hollow is the hollow, deepened.
+static func _digLake(F: WorldField.Field, q: Array, maxr: float, best: int, planLevel: float, level0: float, claimed: Dictionary, cfg: Dictionary) -> Dictionary:
+	_twinMemo.clear()
+	best = _canon(F, best)
+	var fp: Dictionary = _footprint(F, best, planLevel, q, maxr, claimed)
